meta {
  name: Get all projects
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/general/projects
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Get All Projects
  
  Returns a list of all projects, ordered by most recently created and status "ongoing". It also returns the nuber of ongoing projects in the meta object. Results are cached using the `DASHBOARD_CARDS` TTL.
  
  ## Authorization
  
  - **Authentication:** Required — Bearer token via `authenticate()`.
  - **Permission:** `read` — enforced by `authorize("read")`.
  
  ## Request
  
  No path parameters, query parameters, or request body.
  
  ## Response
  
  **`200 OK`** — Returns an array of project records along with useful metadata like the number of ongoing projects.
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": [
      {
        "id": "uuid",
        "title": "Project Title",
        "description": "Project description text",
        "imageUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/...",
        "imagePublicId": "public_id_string",
        "status": "ongoing",
        "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z"
      },
      "meta": {
        "ongoingProjectCount": 4,
    },
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ## Caching
  
  - **Key:** `cedarrise:dashboard:projects`
  - **TTL:** `CACHE_TTL.DASHBOARD_CARDS`
  - Cache is populated on the first successful database fetch; subsequent requests within the TTL window return cached data.
  
  ## Errors
  
  | Status                      | Description                         |
  |-----------------------------|-------------------------------------|
  | `401 Unauthorized`          | Missing or invalid Bearer token.    |
  | `403 Forbidden`             | Insufficient permissions.           |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.            |
}
